# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# claire-test — example environment file
#
# Copy this to `.env` (which is git-ignored) if you want to override a build
# setting locally:  cp .env.example .env
#
# This is a static Vite + React SPA. It has NO backend, database, cache or
# queue, so there are NO runtime secrets — no API keys, no connection strings,
# no tokens. Nothing in this file is sensitive; do not put a real secret here.
#
# The app reads exactly ONE configuration value, and it is a BUILD-TIME setting
# baked into the bundle by Vite — not read from the environment at runtime.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# BASE_URL — the public base path the app is served under.
#
# What it is:   Vite's built-in base path (exposed to code as
#               `import.meta.env.BASE_URL`). Used in src/data/loader.ts to
#               resolve the committed CSVs, e.g. `${BASE_URL}data/sales_weekly.csv`.
# Where it comes from: it is derived from `base` in vite.config.ts (currently
#               "./") or overridden at build time with `vite build --base=/path/`.
#               It is NOT an OS environment variable and NOT read via dotenv;
#               setting it in a `.env` file has no effect at runtime.
# When to change it: only if you deploy the app under a sub-path (e.g. served
#               at https://host/dashboard/ rather than the domain root). Then
#               build with `--base=/dashboard/`. For the default root or the
#               Docker/nginx setup, leave it as "/".
# Default:      /
BASE_URL=/
